text:
Life's Universal Riddle:
we are an imposition on life even as life is an imposition on us;
we are a gratuity on life even as life is a gratuity on us;
we need mercy even as we need to be merciful;
which require affirmative consciousness and fidelity to conscience
- perpetual striving to understand Godlikeness and ever to become more Godlike..

The chart mostly....and its financial data on BMO website.

You know what Warren would say;
“If you've been playing poker for half an hour and you still don't know who the patsy is, you're the patsy.”

In Mr Rosenberg's case...its more like; 
"How much time (as a bear) you wasted "in" the options market" 
 :):)

I don't condone people pretending to be other people on forums like this - it's dishonest and inconsiderate.

That said, for a doppelganger, whoever is spoofing you is doing an excellent job at pointing out the absurdity of most of your posts. 

The logic goes something like this, though I'm sure I'm missing an infinite loop referencing HRC that triggers when the bad news about Trump gets really bad:

if(BadNews==AboutDonald) {News = "OneHundredPercentFake";}
else if(BadNews==AboutHillary) {News = "AbsolutelyTrue";}
else {BadNews = "AboutHillaryOrObamaSomehow";}
